<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
  <title>Conditions — {{BUSINESS_NAME}}</title>
  <style>
    :root{--bg:#fff9f4;--card:#fff;--muted:#5f6b6b;--accent:#8b5e3c;--glass:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);font-family:Georgia,serif}
    body{margin:0;background:linear-gradient(180deg,var(--bg),#fff);color:#222}
    header{position:sticky;top:0;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);backdrop-filter:blur(4px);border-bottom:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.04)}
    .nav{max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:12px}
    .brand{font-weight:700}
    nav a{color:#333;text-decoration:none;padding:8px;border-radius:8px}
    .container{max-width:900px;margin:28px auto;padding:20px}
    h1{font-family:Georgia,serif}
    .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 240px;gap:20px}
    .card{background:var(--card);padding:14px;border-radius:10px;box-shadow:0 8px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.03)}
    .muted{color:var(--muted)}

    .reveal{opacity:0;transform:translateY(12px);transition:opacity 420ms ease,transform 420ms ease}
    .reveal.visible{opacity:1;transform:none}
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){ .reveal{transition:none;opacity:1;transform:none} }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <div class="nav">
      <div class="brand">{{BUSINESS_NAME}}</div>
      <nav style="margin-left:18px">
        <a href="index.html">Home</a>
        <a href="services.html">Services</a>
        <a href="approach.html">Method</a>
        <a href="conditions.html">Conditions</a>
      </nav>
      <div style="margin-left:auto;display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center">
        <a href="book.html" style="background:#f2efe9;padding:8px 12px;border-radius:8px;color:#6b4f3b;text-decoration:none">Book</a>
        <a href="contact.html" style="padding:8px 10px;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none">Contact</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="container">
    <section class="reveal" id="lead">
      <h1>Clinical topics we commonly work with</h1>
      <p class="muted">We support people through patterns like fatigue, sleep disruption, mood variability, digestive trouble, and stress-related pain. Below are brief descriptions and examples of supportive approaches. This information is educational and is not a substitute for personalized medical advice.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="reveal grid" style="margin-top:18px">
      <div>
        <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:12px">
          <h3>Sleep challenges</h3>
          <p class="muted">We explore habits, circadian cues, caffeine & medication timing, and tailored behavioral steps. Interventions may include sleep scheduling, stimulus control, and simple evening routines to support consolidation. In some cases, we collaborate with prescribing clinicians for medication review.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:12px">
          <h3>Persistent fatigue</h3>
          <p class="muted">Fatigue can be multifactorial. We map sleep, mood, nutrition, movement, and medication effects. Lab review and small, measurable experiments help identify what changes best support energy. We do not promise cures — rather, we aim to reduce uncertainty and improve daily function over time.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:12px">
          <h3>Digestive concerns</h3>
          <p class="muted">Work often includes symptom tracking, targeted dietary patterns, and gentle troubleshooting of common issues like bloating or irregularity. When indicated, we coordinate with GI specialists and follow guideline-informed testing.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:12px">
          <h3>Mood and anxiety patterns</h3>
          <p class="muted">We blend practical behavioral strategies, sleep and activity optimization, and collaborative care with mental health clinicians. For people on medications, we communicate with prescribers for safe adjustments when needed.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:12px">
          <h3>Pain and movement</h3>
          <p class="muted">Rather than promising elimination of pain, our focus is on improving movement, function, and strategies to reduce flares using pacing, strengthening, and simple ergonomic changes. We refer for specialized care when necessary.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside>
        <div class="card">
          <h4>Important disclaimers</h4>
          <p class="muted">This page is intended to educate. We do not provide emergency care here. If you have urgent symptoms (chest pain, severe shortness of breath, sudden neurological changes), call emergency services or seek immediate care.</p>
          <p class="muted">Our consultations complement — but do not replace — your existing medical relationships. We may request recent labs or recommend specialist referral when clinically indicated.</p>
          <p class="muted" style="font-weight:700">No guaranteed cures. Individual results vary.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card" style="margin-top:12px">
          <h4>How we choose recommendations</h4>
          <p class="muted">Recommendations are drawn from current evidence, practical experience, and a person’s goals. We prioritize low-burden changes that can be measured and adjusted.</p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="reveal" style="margin-top:18px">
      <h2>When to reach out</h2>
      <p class="muted">If symptoms limit your daily life, create consistent sleep disruption, or you feel stuck despite trying common strategies, a focused consult can help. We can clarify next steps, suggest tracked experiments, and coordinate care with other clinicians.</p>
      <div style="margin-top:12px;display:flex;gap:12px">
        <a href="book.html" style="background:var(--accent);color:white;padding:10px 14px;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none">Request a consultation</a>
        <a href="contact.html" style="padding:10px 14px;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none;background:#f3ede7;color:#7a5b3e;text-decoration:none">Ask a question</a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  <footer style="max-width:900px;margin:20px auto;padding:18px;color:var(--muted)">
    <div>Contact: {{PHONE}} • <a href="mailto:{{EMAIL}}">{{EMAIL}}</a></div>
    <div style="margin-top:6px">Location: {{CITY}}, {{STATE}}</div>
  </footer>

  <script>
    // reveal with reduced motion support
    (function(){
      const prefersReduced = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce)').matches;
      if(prefersReduced){ document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(el=>el.classList.add('visible')); return; }
      const io = new IntersectionObserver((list)=>{ list.forEach(entry=>{ if(entry.isIntersecting){ entry.target.classList.add('visible'); io.unobserve(entry.target); }}); },{threshold:0.08});
      document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(el=>io.observe(el));
    })();
  </script>
</body>
</html>"} 
{"path":"approach.html","content":"<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
  <title>Approach — {{BUSINESS_NAME}}</title>
  <style>
    :root{--bg:#f8fcff;--card:#fff;--muted:#586a6a;--accent:#306c5f;font-family:Inter,system-ui,Segoe UI,Roboto,"Helvetica Neue",Arial}
    body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:#123}
    .wrap{max-width:1100px;margin:28px auto;padding:18px}
